{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rsasaki0109/rustwright/pulls/1","id":4801829552,"node_id":"PR_kwDOUhboA88AAAABHjYasA","html_url":"https://github.com/rsasaki0109/rustwright/pull/1","diff_url":"https://github.com/rsasaki0109/rustwright/pull/1.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/rsasaki0109/rustwright/pull/1.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rsasaki0109/rustwright/issues/1","commits_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rsasaki0109/rustwright/pulls/1/commits","review_comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rsasaki0109/rustwright/pulls/1/comments","review_comment_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rsasaki0109/rustwright/pulls/comments{/number}","comments_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rsasaki0109/rustwright/issues/1/comments","statuses_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/rsasaki0109/rustwright/statuses/be1b065aeff87e5c19e53492a19f4465ba4436f4","number":1,"state":"open","locked":false,"title":"Harden browser reliability and add Firefox network-idle waits","user":{"login":"rsasaki0109","id":18298605,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4Mjk4NjA1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18298605?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsasaki0109","html_url":"https://github.com/rsasaki0109","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsasaki0109/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsasaki0109/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsasaki0109/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsasaki0109/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsasaki0109/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsasaki0109/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsasaki0109/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsasaki0109/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsasaki0109/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Browser cancellation could retain ownership or lose readiness, and explicitly configured legacy startup failures could appear as successful skips. This change makes those failures explicit, hardens page/context/transport/interception cleanup, adds shared reload/history operations, and introduces Firefox network-idle waits through `BidiPage` and `AnyPage`.\n\nFirefox pages acknowledge network observation before handoff. Idle waits track unfinished observed HTTP(S) bodies across nested/cross-origin frames and redirect hops, exclude foreign tabs, preserve monitoring after timeout/cancellation, and report closure, lost events or incomplete cold-context observation explicitly. Every Firefox call starts a fresh 500 ms window; this differs from Chrome's reusable quiet deadline. Twenty-six shared native regressions cover bodies, redirects, frames, replacement navigation, quiet interruption and shutdown. Twenty-two new backend cases cover protocol ordering, acknowledgment, cancellation and ownership.\n\nRequired native CI also exposed browser installation defects. Windows now runs Chrome's official executable-access helper; macOS restores the exact selected official `.app` bundle and framework links; Ubuntu diagnoses explicit sandbox setup failures and installs the byte-identical bundled helper with its required ownership/mode. A real renderer preflight must succeed. Browser sandboxes remain enabled in CI, unexpected errors stay fatal, and failing scenarios are not retried.\n\nValidation at production/test/workflow source `e3bc08e7ce0a117d173bdcde2924165806e8e854`:\n\n- [Run 37974358667](https://github.com/rsasaki0109/rustwright/actions/runs/37974358667): all six jobs succeeded. Chrome 155.0.8059.39 / Firefox 157.0.1 pass 79 required portable native cases on each of Ubuntu, Windows and macOS arm64; zero failed, ignored or filtered. Ubuntu passes another 114 HTTP cases.\n- Full Ubuntu workspace: 453 passed, zero failed/filtered, one existing intentionally ignored macro doctest. This includes 193 library cases (108 BiDi) and 193 HTTP cases. Repeated native jobs overlap this coverage and are not summed as unique tests.\n- Rust 1.85 locked all-target compilation, stable Clippy with warnings denied, formatting and actionlint passed.\n- Eight actual package archives audited; 57 locked dependency checksums verified. Version-only consumers and all nine README Rust fences compile on stable/MSRV. Four native consumer cases, executed macro callbacks and both verbatim README programs pass; five PNGs are retained.\n- Independent local verification: 193 library and 193 HTTP cases plus distribution pass on Chrome 151 / Firefox 157 using container-specific launch adjustments. These results do not imply that local sandbox or every local legacy file/data fixture works.\n- Controlled pre-ACK receiver regressions fail before their correction and pass afterward. The network-idle missing-API baseline is a compilation failure; an intermediate stale-document regression records an actual failing test and its correction.\n\n[CI evidence](https://github.com/rsasaki0109/rustwright/blob/codex/reliability-95-ci/docs/CI_VERIFICATION.md) and [Firefox API scope](https://github.com/rsasaki0109/rustwright/blob/codex/reliability-95-ci/docs/FIREFOX_NETWORK_IDLE_IMPLEMENTATION.md) link frozen before/after records, exact Git source archives, raw logs and SHA256 manifests. Five current remote artifact ZIP digests match GitHub's official API. Later documentation-only commits preserve the evidence; the tested source identity remains the commit above.\n\nRemaining work toward the 95% checkpoint includes memory attribution, lost remote allocation replies/cleanup refusal, representative real sites, headed sessions and broader version coverage. Historical request reconstruction, service-worker/WebSocket tracking and complete backend parity are outside these idle waits' guarantee. Registry publication and a general SOTA claim remain separate; this stays a draft PR.\n","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-10-09T14:31:32Z","updated_at":"2026-10-09T20:29:13Z","closed_at":null,"merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"81864cc233628753cc97cdbb19a70cc30a1d4128","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[],"head":{"label":"rsasaki0109:codex/reliability-95-ci","ref":"codex/reliability-95-ci","repo":{"id":1377232899,"node_id":"R_kgDOUhboAw","name":"rustwright","full_name":"rsasaki0109/rustwright","owner":{"login":"rsasaki0109","id":18298605,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4Mjk4NjA1","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/18298605?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsasaki0109","html_url":"https://github.com/rsasaki0109","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsasaki0109/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsasaki0109/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsasaki0109/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsasaki0109/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsasaki0109/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsasaki0109/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsasaki0109/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsasaki0109/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/rsasaki0109/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"private":false,"fork":false,"archived":false,"disabled":false,"description":"Real-browser-first browser automation for Rust — drives installed Chrome (CDP) and Firefox (WebDriver BiDi) with a Playwright-like async API.","homepage":null,"language":"Rust","visibility":"public","is_template":false,"topics":["browser-automation","chrome-devtools-protocol","firefox","playwright","rust","testing","tokio","webdriver-bidi"],"forks_count":0,"forks":0,"stargazers_count":3,"watchers_count":3,"watchers":3,"open_issues_count":1,"open_issues":1,"size":11029,"default_branch"